)ATTR DEFAULT(@}_)
 @ TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(WHITE)
 } TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(LOW)  COLOR(GREEN)
 { TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(LOW)  COLOR(TURQ)
 _ TYPE(INPUT)  INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(RED)    CAPS(ON) JUST(LEFT)
 ! TYPE(OUTPUT) INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(YELLOW) CAPS(OFF) JUST(LEFT)
)BODY
@HELP: Printer Panel -- Action Characters       !ISFHMSG                      }
@COMMAND INPUT ===>_ISFHCMD                                                   }
}  Type an action character in the NP column of a printer and press
}  Enter. Each gives JES2 the command named for that printer.
}
{   D  }Display the printer ($DU).
{   S  }Start the printer ($S).
{   P  }Stop the printer when the output it prints is done ($P).
{   Z  }Halt the printer at once; S lets it go on ($Z).
{   I  }Interrupt the output it prints; it is printed again later ($I).
{   E  }Restart the output it prints from the beginning ($E).
{   C  }Cancel the output it prints ($C).
{   N  }Print one more copy of the output it prints ($N).
{   Bn }Backspace: B5 goes back 5 pages ($B). D and C as JES2 takes them.
{   Fn }Forward space: F5 skips 5 pages ($F). D and C the same way.
}
}  JES2's answers go to the system log; the panel says COMMAND ISSUED.
}  Enter shows the new state of the printers.
}
}  D needs READ access to SDSF.OPER, the others UPDATE access. Without
}  it: NOT AUTHORIZED FOR PRT.
}
}
}  Enter: next topic   PF7: Printer panel help   PF3: back to SDSF
)PROC
  &ISFHPFK = .PFKEY
  &ZCONT = ISFHPRF
  &ZUP = ISFHPR
)END
